# The F-22A's control surfaces (src/gfx/parts.hpp says how a line is
# read): each a hinge line from its inboard or lower end to its other, in the
# model's body frame, metres from its origin - +x forward, +y starboard, +z
# down - then how far forward of the hinge the part reaches, how far aft, and
# how far either side of the hinge's plane; and first the JSBSim property
# whose value, in radians, is its deflection, with which way a positive value
# moves its trailing edge.
#
# Measured off the model's own sections (assets/models/f22.mesh), by
# slicing it where each surface ends: the ailerons between 68% and 90% of the
# wing's semispan, each hinge a quarter of the local chord forward of the
# trailing edge;
# the all-moving tailplane from 2.0 m out to 3.2 m, pivoted a quarter of
# its chord aft of its leading edge;
# each rudder, on its own fin, from 0.3 m above the origin to 2.2 m,
# hinged three tenths of the chord forward of the trailing edge.
# The sections each was measured from are above its lines.
#
# wing -5.60..-1.35 at 4.61 m, -5.00..-2.72 at 6.10 m
surface left-aileron    fcs/left-aileron-pos-rad   down  -4.538 -4.610 0.594  -4.432 -6.102 0.634  0.000 1.243 0.206
surface right-aileron   fcs/right-aileron-pos-rad  down  -4.538 4.610 0.594  -4.432 6.102 0.634  0.000 1.243 0.206
# tail -8.86..-5.59 at 2.00 m, -9.33..-6.65 at 3.20 m
surface left-elevator   fcs/elevator-pos-rad       down  -6.408 -2.000 0.467  -7.320 -3.200 0.465  0.960 2.839 0.102
surface right-elevator  fcs/elevator-pos-rad       down  -6.408 2.000 0.467  -7.320 3.200 0.465  0.960 2.839 0.102
# fin -7.60..-6.72 at -0.30 m, -6.70..-5.75 at -2.20 m
surface left-rudder     fcs/rudder-pos-rad         right -7.334 -1.718 -0.300  -6.411 -2.858 -2.200  0.000 0.348 0.104
# fin -7.60..-6.72 at -0.30 m, -6.70..-5.76 at -2.20 m
surface right-rudder    fcs/rudder-pos-rad         right -7.334 1.717 -0.300  -6.415 2.856 -2.200  0.000 0.343 0.104
